#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/any-trait.md:33
msgid ""
"The `Any` trait allows us to downcast values back from dyn values into "
"concrete values."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/any-trait.md:36
msgid ""
"This is an auto trait: like Send/Sync/Sized, it is automatically implemented "
"for any type that meets specific criteria."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/any-trait.md:39
msgid ""
"The criteria for Any is that a type is `'static`. That is, the type does not "
"contain any non-`'static` lifetimes within it."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/any-trait.md:42
msgid ""
"Any offers two related behaviors: downcasting, and runtime checking of types "
"being the same."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/any-trait.md:45
msgid ""
"In the example above, we see the ability to downcast from `Any` into "
"`ThisImplementsAny` automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/any-trait.md:48
msgid ""
"We also see `Any::is` being used to check to see what type the value is."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/from-oop-to-rust/dynamic-dispatch/any-trait.md:50
msgid ""
"`Any` does not implement reflection for a type, this is all you can do with "
"`Any`."
msgstr ""
